From: Meerzulee <17146298+meerzulee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: 74x164: add TI SN74HC164 compatible

The Archer C58HP drives its LED shift register with SPI GPIO clock and
data lines, without a chip-select or storage-register latch. The existing
74x164 driver can transfer the register contents in this configuration.
Add explicit device matches and document the absence of a latch on the
SN74HC164; no transfer algorithm changes are needed.

---
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-74x164.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-74x164.c
@@ -167,6 +167,7 @@ static int gen_74x164_probe(struct spi_d
 static const struct spi_device_id gen_74x164_spi_ids[] = {
 	{ .name = "74hc595" },
 	{ .name = "74lvc594" },
+	{ .name = "sn74hc164" },
 	{},
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(spi, gen_74x164_spi_ids);
@@ -174,6 +175,7 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(spi, gen_74x164_spi_
 static const struct of_device_id gen_74x164_dt_ids[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "fairchild,74hc595" },
 	{ .compatible = "nxp,74lvc594" },
+	{ .compatible = "ti,sn74hc164" },
 	{},
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, gen_74x164_dt_ids);
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/fairchild,74hc595.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/fairchild,74hc595.yaml
@@ -23,6 +23,9 @@ description: |
   chip select#      |___________________|
 
 
+  The SN74HC164 has no storage-register latch. Its outputs follow the shift
+  register during a transfer; use it without a chip-select/latch clock.
+
 maintainers:
   - Maxime Ripard <mripard@kernel.org>
 
@@ -31,6 +34,7 @@ properties:
     enum:
       - fairchild,74hc595
       - nxp,74lvc594
+      - ti,sn74hc164
 
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
